# Trivy ignore policy for Grok Bot trading service
#
# SECURITY CONTEXT & THREAT MODEL:
# The Grok Bot trading service runs in a controlled Docker environment with:
# - No untrusted input parsing (only API calls to known endpoints)
# - No deserialization of untrusted data
# - No public-facing network interfaces (internal service)
# - Fixed operation: fetch data, filter, make trading decisions
# - Single-user/single-purpose application
#
# ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:
# We accept CVEs in Python/system dependencies when:
# 1. The vulnerability requires input vectors we don't expose (e.g., web parsing,
#    file upload, untrusted deserialization)
# 2. The vulnerability is in a transitive dependency and the attack chain is
#    not realistic in our context
# 3. The vulnerable code path is not reachable in our usage pattern
# 4. No viable patched version exists (documented with reason)
#
# Python PACKAGE VULNERABILITIES (Context-specific):
# Most Python package CVEs fall into categories not exploitable here:
# - SSRF/URL parsing: We only call pre-configured API endpoints
# - Deserialization attacks: We only call APIs with known JSON schemas
# - Input validation bypasses: Our inputs are API responses, not user-controlled
# - Dependency chain issues: We accept lower-priority CVEs in transitive deps
#
# FORMAT:
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN  # CONTEXT: Brief explanation why this is acceptable in our context
#
# CURRENT STATUS: Awaiting detailed CVE analysis from Trivy output
# (Add specific CVE entries as needed based on actual scan findings)
